[00:14.34] Grass in your hair stretched like a lion in the sun
[00:23.01] Restlessly turned, moistened your mouth with your tongue
[00:34.33] Pouring my wine, your eyes caged mine glowing
[00:45.16] Touching your face, my finger strayed knowing
[00:54.55] I called you lady of the dancing water
[01:02.25] 
[01:29.55] Oh lovely lady of the dancing water
[01:37.24] 
[01:42.30] Blown autumn leaves shed to the fire where you laid
[01:53.66] Burn slow to ash just as my days now seem to be
[02:04.20] I feel you still, always your eyes glowing
[02:14.29] Remembered hours, salt, earth, and flowers flowing
[02:24.06] Farewell my lady of the dancing water
[02:31.08] 